      "exact_html": "<p id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">On this class, exact first-order access is equivalent to exact\nmatrix–vector access.\nIndeed, a first-order response contains <math id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"Ax\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Ax</annotation></semantics></math>, while a\nmatrix–vector response determines both the gradient <math id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"Ax\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">Ax</annotation></semantics></math>\nand the function value <math id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\frac{1}{2}\\langle x,Ax\\rangle\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{1}{2}\\langle x,Ax\\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>.\nThus the exact value-and-gradient, gradient-only, and\nmatrix–vector query complexities coincide.</p>",
      "rendered_text": "On this class, exact first-order access is equivalent to exact\nmatrix–vector access.\nIndeed, a first-order response contains A ​ x Ax , while a\nmatrix–vector response determines both the gradient A ​ x Ax and the function value 1 2 ​ ⟨ x , A ​ x ⟩ \\frac{1}{2}\\langle x,Ax\\rangle .\nThus the exact value-and-gradient, gradient-only, and\nmatrix–vector query complexities coincide.",
      "latex_alttexts": [
        "Ax",
        "Ax",
        "\\frac{1}{2}\\langle x,Ax\\rangle"
      ]
