      "exact_html": "<p id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">A randomized algorithm chooses its queries and stopping decisions\nas Borel functions of its internal randomness and previous oracle\nresponses, where the randomness is independent of the input.\nIts output may be any <math id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\mathbb{R}^{d}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>-valued Borel function of\nthe same information.\nThe algorithm has <em id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1\" class=\"ltx_emph ltx_font_italic\">fixed query budget</em> <math id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"T\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math> if it makes\nat most <math id=\"S2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"T\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math> queries for every admissible input and every\nrealization of its internal randomness.</p>",
      "rendered_text": "A randomized algorithm chooses its queries and stopping decisions\nas Borel functions of its internal randomness and previous oracle\nresponses, where the randomness is independent of the input.\nIts output may be any ℝ d \\mathbb{R}^{d} -valued Borel function of\nthe same information.\nThe algorithm has fixed query budget T T if it makes\nat most T T queries for every admissible input and every\nrealization of its internal randomness.",
