      "exact_html": "<div id=\"S4.p2\" class=\"ltx_para\">\n<p id=\"S4.p2.1\" class=\"ltx_p\">Compared with Theorem <a href=\"#S3.Thmtheorem1\" title=\"Theorem 3.1 (Gaussian sampling lower bound). ‣ 3 Lower Bound via Hidden Determinant Sign ‣ On Complexity of Gaussian Sampling\" class=\"ltx_ref\"><span class=\"ltx_text ltx_ref_tag\">3.1</span></a>, this bound also covers <math id=\"S4.p2.m1\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"2\\leq\\kappa&lt;4\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">2\\leq\\kappa&lt;4</annotation></semantics></math> and\n<math id=\"S4.p2.m2\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\frac{1}{16}&lt;\\varepsilon\\leq\\frac{1}{10}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>16</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>10</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\frac{1}{16}&lt;\\varepsilon\\leq\\frac{1}{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, and it holds even when the spectrum of <math id=\"S4.p2.m3\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"A\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">A</annotation></semantics></math> is known to\nthe algorithm. On the other hand, it does not grow as <math id=\"S4.p2.m4\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\varepsilon\\to 0\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\varepsilon\\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> and it requires <math id=\"S4.p2.m5\" class=\"ltx_Math\" alttext=\"\\kappa\\leq d^{1-\\delta}\" display=\"inline\" intent=\":literal\"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\kappa\\leq d^{1-\\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>\n</div>",
      "rendered_text": "Compared with Theorem 3.1 , this bound also covers 2 ≤ κ < 4 2\\leq\\kappa<4 and 1 16 < ε ≤ 1 10 \\frac{1}{16}<\\varepsilon\\leq\\frac{1}{10} , and it holds even when the spectrum of A A is known to\nthe algorithm. On the other hand, it does not grow as ε → 0 \\varepsilon\\to 0 and it requires κ ≤ d 1 − δ \\kappa\\leq d^{1-\\delta} .",
